 \n \n \n \n  \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "RFP Title Year/Contract Start Reference", :date "2025", :evidence "2025 Parking Management Services"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Issuing Authority", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"}], :financials [{:item "Contract Price", :amount_or_terms "See Part 2 (Page 3)", :evidence "PART 2  CONTRACT PRICE         3"} {:item "Payment Terms", :amount_or_terms "See Schedule 'C' (Page 28)", :evidence "Schedule 'C' Payment Terms          28"} {:item "Contract Security & Insurance", :amount_or_terms "See Schedule 'D' (Page 35)", :evidence "Schedule 'D' Contract Security & Insurance         35"}], :summary_points ["This page serves as the Table of Contents and cover page for the 2025 Parking Management Services Contract/RFP for Victoria Airport Authority." "The document structure includes Articles of Agreement followed by five schedules (A through E)." "Specific sections are dedicated to defining the Scope of Work, Payment Terms, and General Conditions of the contract." "Detailed provisions for Contract Price and Contract Representatives are located in Parts 2 and 3 of the Articles of Agreement."]}} {:page-number 71, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 71\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 2 of 67 \n \nThese Articles of Agreement dated for reference the _______ day of _____________2025. \n \nBETWEEN:   \nVICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY \nVictoria International Airport  \n201 - 1640 Electra Blvd.  \nSidney, BC V8L 5V4 \n \nAttention:  \nEmail:  legalnotice@victoriaairport.com      \n(the “VAA”) \n \nAND    \n[CONTRACTOR’S LEGAL NAME] \n[STREET ADDRESS] \n[CITY, PROVINCE, POSTAL CODE] \n \nAttention:  \nEmail:  \n(the “Contractor”) \n \nTHE PARTIES HEREBY AGREE AS FOLLOWS: \n \nARTICLES OF AGREEMENT \n \nPART 1 – CONTRACT DOCUMENTS \n \n1.1 The following documents form the Contract (the \"Contract\") between the VAA and the Contractor: \n \n• These Articles of Agreement  \n• The attached Schedule 'A' -Definitions; \n• The attached Schedule 'B' - Scope of Work; \n• The attached Schedule 'C'- Payment Conditions; \n• The attached Schedule 'D'- Contract Security & Insurance; \n• The attached Schedule 'E'- General Conditions; and \n• Any amendment or variation of the Contract that is made in accordance with the GC 1.1 of Schedule 'E'. \n \n1.2 The Contract Documents as a whole will constitute the Contract between the parties and will, subject to \nthe provisions of this Contract and the law, enure for the benefit of and be binding upon the parties hereto, \ntheir respective administrators, successors, and permitted assigns. \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Articles of Agreement Reference Date", :date "2025-01-01", :time nil, :timezone nil, :evidence "These Articles of Agreement dated for reference the _______ day of _____________2025."}], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "VAA", :contact "201 - 1640 Electra Blvd., Sidney, BC V8L 5V4; legalnotice@victoriaairport.com", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY... Victoria International Airport... 201 - 1640 Electra Blvd. Sidney, BC V8L 5V4... Email: legalnotice@victoriaairport.com (the “VAA”)"} {:name "[CONTRACTOR’S LEGAL NAME]", :role "Contractor", :contact "[STREET ADDRESS], [CITY, PROVINCE, POSTAL CODE]", :evidence "[CONTRACTOR’S LEGAL NAME]... [STREET ADDRESS]... (the “Contractor”)"}], :financials [], :summary_points ["This page serves as the formal Articles of Agreement for the 2025 Parking Management Services RFP at Victoria International Airport." "The contract structure is defined by the Articles of Agreement and five specific schedules (A through E) covering definitions, scope, payment, security/insurance, and general conditions." "The agreement is legally binding upon the parties, including their successors and permitted assigns."]}} {:page-number 72, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 72\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 3 of 67 \n \n \nPART 2 – CONTRACT PRICE \n \n2.1  MANAGEMENT FEE \n2.1.1 As compensation for the Contractor's Work, the VAA will pay the Contractor a fixed Management Fee for \neach year of the Term in accordance with the payment conditions set out in Schedule 'C', in the following \namounts (shown as both annual and monthly amounts): \nContract Year Annual \nAmount \nMonthly Amount \n2025-June-01 to 2026-May-\n31 \n \n \n2026-June-01 to 2027-May-\n31 \n \n \n2027-June-01 to 2028-May-\n31 \n \n \n2028-June-01 to 2029-May-\n31 \n \n \n2029-June-01 to 2030-May-\n31 \n \n \n \n2.1.2 If, during the Term of the Contract, the Contractor’s staff organize or join a bargaining labour union, the \nContractor will be responsible for meeting the demands of the union, and VAA will not be required to agree \nto any increase in the Management Fee, or any part thereof, based on any such labour union negotiations. \n \n2.2 FEDERAL GOODS AND SERVICES TAX (GST) \n2.2.1 GST will be payable on the purchase of goods and on the provision of services supplied in Canada or \nimported, except for those specifically declared in the Act to be tax-free or tax-exempt. \n2.2.2 GST is excluded from the prices and rates quoted herein.  Any amount to be levied against the VAA in \nrespect of the GST is to be shown separately on all invoices for goods or services supplied.  The Contractor \nagrees to include the Contractor's GST Registration Number on all invoices and to remit to Revenue Canada \nany GST paid or due. \n \nPART 3 – CONTRACT REPRESENTATIVES \n \n3.1 The VAA designates TBD, as their contract representative for the purposes of this Contract, whose address \nis as follows: \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Contract Year 1 Start", :date "2025-06-01", :evidence "2025-June-01 to 2026-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 1 End", :date "2026-05-31", :evidence "2025-June-01 to 2026-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 2 Start", :date "2026-06-01", :evidence "2026-June-01 to 2027-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 2 End", :date "2027-05-31", :evidence "2026-June-01 to 2027-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 3 Start", :date "2027-06-01", :evidence "2027-June-01 to 2028-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 3 End", :date "2028-05-31", :evidence "2027-June-01 to 2028-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 4 Start", :date "2028-06-01", :evidence "2028-June-01 to 2029-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 4 End", :date "2029-05-31", :evidence "2028-June-01 to 2029-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 5 Start", :date "2029-06-01", :evidence "2029-June-01 to 2030-May-31"} {:name "Contract Year 5 End", :date "2030-05-31", :evidence "2029-June-01 to 2030-May-31"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / VAA", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "the VAA will pay the Contractor a fixed Management Fee"} {:name "Revenue Canada", :role "Tax Authority", :evidence "remit to Revenue Canada any GST paid or due"} {:name "TBD", :role "Contract Representative", :evidence "The VAA designates TBD, as their contract representative"}], :financials [{:item "Management Fee", :amount_or_terms "Fixed annual and monthly amounts for each year of the Term", :evidence "the VAA will pay the Contractor a fixed Management Fee for each year of the Term... (shown as both annual and monthly amounts)"} {:item "Labour Union Negotiation Costs", :amount_or_terms "VAA not required to increase Management Fee due to labour union demands", :evidence "VAA will not be required to agree to any increase in the Management Fee, or any part thereof, based on any such labour union negotiations."} {:item "Federal Goods and Services Tax (GST)", :amount_or_terms "Payable on goods/services; excluded from quoted prices; must be shown separately on invoices", :evidence "GST is excluded from the prices and rates quoted herein. Any amount to be levied against the VAA in respect of the GST is to be shown separately on all invoices"}], :summary_points ["The contract defines a fixed management fee structure spanning five years from June 1, 2025, to May 31, 2030." "Management fees are fixed and will not be adjusted if the contractor's staff engages in labor union negotiations or collective bargaining." "GST is not included in the primary quoted rates and must be invoiced separately with the contractor's GST Registration Number." "The VAA will designate a specific contract representative, though the individual is currently listed as To Be Determined (TBD)."]}} {:page-number 73, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 73\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 4 of 67 \n \nVictoria Airport Authority  \n201 - 1640 Electra Blvd.  \nSidney, BC   V8L 5V4 \n \nTelephone No: TBD \nCell Phone:  TBD \nEmail: TBD  \n \n3.2 The Contractor designates [insert name and title], as their contract representative for the purposes of this \nContract, whose address is as follows: \n \n[CONTRACTOR NAME AND ADDRESS] \n \nTelephone No.  \nCell No.  \nEmail:   \n \n3.3 Both contract representatives or their designated alternate will have full authority of their respective party \nto deal with all matters arising under this Contract. \n \n \nPART 4 – PERFORMANCE OF THE WORK \n \n4.1 The Contractor will perform and complete the Work required by this Contract with all due care, skill, \ndiligence and efficiency in a good and workmanlike manner, to the full satisfaction of the VAA. \n \n4.2 The Contractor will do and fulfill everything that is required by this Contract. \n4.3 The Contractor further warrants that: \na) it is fully competent and qualified to perform the Work required under this Contract; and \n \nb) all personnel assigned to perform the Work have the necessary qualifications, knowledge, skill and \nability to perform the Work. \n \n \nPART 5 – TERM OF THE CONTRACT  \n \n5.1 This Contract is for an initial Term of Five (5) years beginning June 1, 2025, and ending May 31, 2030 (the \n“Initial Term”) subject to renewal as herein provided in Clause 5.2. The Initial Term and any renewal or \nextension thereof shall collectively constitute the “Term”). \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Initial Term Start Date", :date "2025-06-01", :evidence "Term of Five (5) years beginning June 1, 2025"} {:name "Initial Term End Date", :date "2030-05-31", :evidence "ending May 31, 2030 (the “Initial Term”)"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / VAA", :contact "201 - 1640 Electra Blvd. Sidney, BC V8L 5V4", :evidence "Victoria Airport Authority 201 - 1640 Electra Blvd. Sidney, BC V8L 5V4"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "The Contractor designates [insert name and title], as their contract representative"}], :financials [], :summary_points ["The contract for 2025 Parking Management Services has an initial term of five years, specifically from June 1, 2025, to May 31, 2030." "Both the Victoria Airport Authority (VAA) and the Contractor must designate contract representatives with full authority to manage contract matters." "The Contractor warrants that they and their personnel are fully competent, qualified, and skilled to perform the required work to the satisfaction of the VAA."]}} {:page-number 74, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 74\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 5 of 67 \n \n \n5.2 If, at the expiration of the Initial Term of this Contract, the VAA desires a renewal of this Contract for a \nsecond Term of two (2) years beginning June 1, 2030, the VAA will not later than December 1, 2029, six (6) \nmonths before such expiration, give notice in writing of such desire to the Contractor. If the Contractor \ndesires such a renewal, the VAA will then grant a renewal of this Contract for a second Term of two (2) \nyears, beginning June 1, 2030, and ending May 31, 2032 (the “Renewal Term”) on such terms and conditions \nas the VAA and the Contractor mutually agree. \n \nEXECUTED by the parties as at the date first written above. \n \nVICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY \n \n \n  \nElizabeth M. Brown, President and CEO \n \n \n[CONTRACTOR] \n \n \n \n  \nName: \nTitle: \n  \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Start of Renewal Term", :date "2030-06-01", :evidence "beginning June 1, 2030"} {:name "Deadline for VAA renewal notice", :date "2029-12-01", :evidence "the VAA will not later than December 1, 2029, six (6) months before such expiration, give notice in writing"} {:name "End of Renewal Term", :date "2032-05-31", :evidence "ending May 31, 2032"}], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Authority / VAA", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY"} {:name "Elizabeth M. Brown", :role "President and CEO", :evidence "Elizabeth M. Brown, President and CEO"} {:name "[CONTRACTOR]", :role "Contractor", :evidence "[CONTRACTOR]"}], :financials [], :summary_points ["Defines a two-year Renewal Term option for the Parking Management Services contract extending from June 1, 2030, to May 31, 2032." "Establishes a notification deadline of December 1, 2029, for the VAA to signal intent to renew." "Specifies that renewal terms and conditions must be mutually agreed upon by the VAA and the Contractor." "Provides the signature block for the formal execution of the agreement by the VAA President and CEO and the Contractor."]}} {:page-number 75, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 75\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 6 of 67 \n \n \nPARKING MANAGEMENT SERVICES CONTRACT \n \nSCHEDULE 'A' \n \nDEFINITIONS \n \nThe following definitions will apply to all Contract Documents: \n \n\"Airport\" means the Victoria International Airport. \n \n\"Annual Gross Revenue Statement\" means the Gross Revenue detail to be provided by the Contractor to the VAA \nannually and referred to in Clause 1.3.3 of Schedule 'C'. \n \n“Authority” means the Victoria Airport Authority. “Authority”, “Airport Authority”, and “VAA” shall have \nequivalent meanings. \n \n\"Business Days\" means any day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or a statutory holiday observed in British \nColumbia and \"Business Day\" will have a corresponding meaning. \n \n\"Canadian Transportation Agency\" means the agency designated under the Canada Transport Act to implement \nthe federal government's transportation policy. \n \n\"CCTV\" means closed circuit television system. \n \n\"Commercial Vehicle Lane\" means the parking lane as more particularly shown on the drawing attached To the \nRFP as Appendix A – YYJ PARKING FACILITIES. \n \n\"Contract\" has the meaning ascribed to it in Part 1 of the Articles of Agreement. \n \n\"Contract Documents\" means this Contract and includes all the documents listed in Part 1 of the Articles of \nAgreement and subsequent written amendments thereto made pursuant to the provisions of this Contract and \nsigned by the parties. \n \n\"Contract Manager\" means the person designated pursuant to Clause GC 3.1 of Schedule 'E' and in charge of the \nday-to-day performance of the Work by the Contractor. \n \n\"Contract Year\" means, in the case of first Contract Year, the period commencing on the first day of the first \nmonth of the Term referred to in Clause 5.1 and terminating on the last day of the twelfth (12) calendar month of \nthe Term and in the case of each subsequent Contract Year means each twelve (12) month period after the first \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / VAA", :evidence "“Authority” means the Victoria Airport Authority. “Authority”, “Airport Authority”, and “VAA” shall have equivalent meanings."} {:name "Canadian Transportation Agency", :role "Agency designated under the Canada Transport Act to implement the federal government's transportation policy", :evidence "\"Canadian Transportation Agency\" means the agency designated under the Canada Transport Act to implement the federal government's transportation policy."} {:name "Contractor", :role "Provider of the Work and Annual Gross Revenue Statement", :evidence "\"Annual Gross Revenue Statement\" means the Gross Revenue detail to be provided by the Contractor to the VAA... \"Contract Manager\" means the person... in charge of the day-to-day performance of the Work by the Contractor."} {:name "Contract Manager", :role "Person in charge of the day-to-day performance of the Work by the Contractor", :evidence "\"Contract Manager\" means the person designated pursuant to Clause GC 3.1 of Schedule 'E' and in charge of the day-to-day performance of the Work by the Contractor."}], :financials [{:item "Annual Gross Revenue Statement", :amount_or_terms "Gross Revenue detail to be provided by the Contractor to the VAA annually", :evidence "\"Annual Gross Revenue Statement\" means the Gross Revenue detail to be provided by the Contractor to the VAA annually and referred to in Clause 1.3.3 of Schedule 'C'."}], :summary_points ["This page defines key terms for the 2025 Parking Management Services Contract at Victoria International Airport." "Defines a 'Contract Year' as a twelve-month period starting from the first day of the first month of the Term." "Establishes 'Business Days' as excluding Saturdays, Sundays, and statutory holidays in British Columbia." "Outlines the requirement for an 'Annual Gross Revenue Statement' to be submitted by the Contractor to the Victoria Airport Authority."]}} {:page-number 76, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 76\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 7 of 67 \n \nContract Year. \n \n\"Contractor\" means ____________________________ and includes any of its successor or permitted assigns and \nalso means any directors, officers, servants, employees, agents, Subcontractors or suppliers of the Contractor and \nany other Person for whom the Contractor may be responsible for in law. \n \n“Contractor’s Proposal” means the Contractor’s response, dated ___ day of _____________ 2025, to the VAA’s \nRFP issued on the 13th day of February, 2025, a copy of which Proposal is annexed to and forms an integral part \nof this Contract as Appendix C to Schedule B. \n \n\"Credit Card Processing Fees” means the standard credit card processing fee paid when accepting credit card \npayments.  \n \n\"Crown\" means His Majesty the King in Right of Canada as represented by the Minister of Transport. \n \n“Curb Management Program” is the system whereby Curb Management Officers monitor and manage the flow \nof vehicles on the shared use curbs on the terminal frontage and in the commercial lane of the short-term parking \nlot.  \n \n“Curbside Management Officer” and “CMO” is an employee of the Contractor trained to monitor and manage \nthe flow of vehicles on the shared use curbs on the terminal frontage and in the commercial lane of the short-\nterm parking lot. \n \n\"Daily Parking Lot\" means the parking lot as more particularly shown on the drawing attached to the RFP as \nAppendix A – YYJ PARKING FACILITIES. \n \n\"Days\" means calendar days including Saturday, Sunday and statutory holidays observed in British Columbia. \n \n\"Employee Parking Lot\" means the parking lot as more particularly shown on the drawing attached to the RFP as \nAppendix A – YYJ PARKING FACILITIES. \n \n\"Financial Statements\" means the Weekly Statement of Revenue, Monthly Statement of Account and Annual \nGross Revenue Statement. \n \n\"Gross Revenue\" means all the Monies collected by the Contractor from the operation of the Parking Facilities \nand any other income generated as a result of this Contract, including without limitation: \n \na) all amounts collected by the Contractor under this Contract where such amounts are collected at a place \nother than the Parking Facilities; \n \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "RFP Issue Date", :date "2025-02-13", :evidence "VAA’s RFP issued on the 13th day of February, 2025"} {:name "Contractor's Proposal Date", :date "2025-01-01", :evidence "Contractor’s response, dated ___ day of _____________ 2025"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Issuing Authority (VAA)", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "\"Contractor\" means ____________________________ and includes any of its successor or permitted assigns"} {:name "Crown", :role "His Majesty the King in Right of Canada", :evidence "\"Crown\" means His Majesty the King in Right of Canada as represented by the Minister of Transport."} {:name "Minister of Transport", :role "Representative of the Crown", :evidence "as represented by the Minister of Transport."} {:name "Curbside Management Officer", :role "Contractor employee (CMO)", :evidence "“Curbside Management Officer” and “CMO” is an employee of the Contractor"}], :financials [{:item "Credit Card Processing Fees", :amount_or_terms "Standard credit card processing fee paid when accepting credit card payments.", :evidence "\"Credit Card Processing Fees” means the standard credit card processing fee paid when accepting credit card payments."} {:item "Gross Revenue", :amount_or_terms "All Monies collected by the Contractor from the operation of the Parking Facilities and any other income generated as a result of this Contract, including amounts collected off-site.", :evidence "\"Gross Revenue\" means all the Monies collected by the Contractor from the operation of the Parking Facilities and any other income generated as a result of this Contract... including... all amounts collected by the Contractor under this Contract where such amounts are collected at a place other than the Parking Facilities"} {:item "Financial Statements", :amount_or_terms "Includes Weekly Statement of Revenue, Monthly Statement of Account and Annual Gross Revenue Statement.", :evidence "\"Financial Statements\" means the Weekly Statement of Revenue, Monthly Statement of Account and Annual Gross Revenue Statement."}], :summary_points ["Defines key terms for the 2025 Parking Management Services contract at Victoria Airport (YYJ)." "Outlines the responsibilities for the Curb Management Program and the role of Curbside Management Officers (CMO)." "Specifies reporting requirements including weekly, monthly, and annual financial statements for gross revenue." "Clarifies that 'Days' includes Saturdays, Sundays, and statutory holidays in British Columbia."]}} {:page-number 77, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 77\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 8 of 67 \n \nb) all amounts that are lost due to theft or defalcation; and \n \nc) all sales taxes at the retailer level, the amount of which is determined by the amount of sales made and \nwhich is required to be collected and accounted for to any provincial or municipal authority; \n \nHowever, the Contractor may deduct the standard Credit Card Processing Fees from the Gross Revenue paid to \nthe VAA by the Contractor. \n \nIn all cases where the Gross Revenue derived from operation of the Parking Facilities by the Contractor is not \ncollected by the Contractor at the time such payment is due, all such amounts will not be accounted for by the \nContractor, as Gross Revenue, until such time as payment thereof has been received by the Contractor. \n \n“Head Lease” means that lease agreement dated for reference the 1st day of April 1997, as amended from time \nto time, by which His Majesty the King in Right of Canada as represented by the Minister of Transport leased to \nthe VAA certain lands and premises as described therein (the “Airport Lands”), encompassing the property \ngenerally known and described as the Victoria International Airport, (the “Airport”). \n \n\"Interest\" means the VAA's rate of interest, which is equal to 2% per month, compounded monthly (26.824% per \nyear). \n \n\"Letter of Credit\" means the irrevocable, unconditional letter of credit referred to in Clause 1.1 of Schedule 'D'. \n \n\"Management Fee” means the amount payable by the VAA to the Contractor as set out in Part 2.1.1 of the Articles \nof Agreement. \n \n\"Monies\" means all payments received and collected from the operation of the Parking Facilities in the form of \ncash, credit cards, debit cards, cheques, electronic transactions, and any other form of legal payment. \n \n\"Monthly Statement of Account\" means the accounting detail to be provided by the Contractor monthly to the \nVAA and referred to in Clause 1.3. 2 of Schedule 'C'. \n \n\"Parking Facilities\" means any and all parking areas in the vicinity of the Air Terminal Building at the Victoria \nInternational Airport which is subject to change from time to time. The Parking Facilities are further described in \nClause 4.3.1 of Schedule 'B' of this Contract, and include the Short-Term Parking Lot, Long-Term Parking Lot 1, \nLong-Term Parking Lot 2, Employee Parking Lot, and the Commercial Vehicle Lane, all as being more particularly \nshown on the drawing attached to the RFP as Appendix A – YYJ PARKING FACILITIES. \n \n\"Parking Fees\" means the fees referred to in Clause 2.9.2 of Schedule 'B', and as set out in more detail in Appendix \nB to the RFP – PARKING LOT RATES, and which Parking Fees shall be inclusive of all applicable taxes. \n \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Head Lease Reference Date", :date "1997-04-01", :evidence "“Head Lease” means that lease agreement dated for reference the 1st day of April 1997"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / VAA", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "His Majesty the King in Right of Canada", :role "Lessor in Head Lease", :evidence "His Majesty the King in Right of Canada as represented by the Minister of Transport leased to the VAA"} {:name "Minister of Transport", :role "Representative of His Majesty the King", :evidence "as represented by the Minister of Transport"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "the Contractor may deduct the standard Credit Card Processing Fees from the Gross Revenue"}], :financials [{:item "Deduction from Gross Revenue", :amount_or_terms "Standard Credit Card Processing Fees", :evidence "the Contractor may deduct the standard Credit Card Processing Fees from the Gross Revenue paid to the VAA"} {:item "Interest Rate", :amount_or_terms "2% per month, compounded monthly (26.824% per year)", :evidence "\"Interest\" means the VAA's rate of interest, which is equal to 2% per month, compounded monthly (26.824% per year)."} {:item "Management Fee", :amount_or_terms "As set out in Part 2.1.1 of the Articles of Agreement", :evidence "\"Management Fee” means the amount payable by the VAA to the Contractor as set out in Part 2.1.1 of the Articles of Agreement."} {:item "Taxes", :amount_or_terms "Inclusive of all applicable taxes", :evidence "\"Parking Fees\" means the fees... which Parking Fees shall be inclusive of all applicable taxes."} {:item "Excluded from Gross Revenue", :amount_or_terms "Theft, defalcation, and sales taxes", :evidence "all amounts that are lost due to theft or defalcation; and c) all sales taxes at the retailer level"}], :summary_points ["Defines key financial terms including Gross Revenue, Management Fees, and a 2% monthly interest rate on VAA accounts." "Specifies that the Contractor can deduct standard Credit Card Processing Fees from the Gross Revenue paid to the VAA." "Identifies the primary parking facilities including Short-Term, Long-Term (1 and 2), Employee lots, and the Commercial Vehicle Lane." "Establishes the legal basis for the airport lands via a 1997 Head Lease between the VAA and the Government of Canada."]}} {:page-number 78, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 78\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 9 of 67 \n \n\"Parking Transactions\" shall mean the sum of the number of times in any one-week period that the vend arm of \nthe incoming entrance gates to the Short Term Parking Lot is activated plus the number of times the vend arm of \nthe outgoing exit gates from the Daily Parking Lot is activated. \n \n\"Person\" means any individual, company, corporation, partnership, firm, trust, sole proprietorship, government \nor government agency, authority or entity, however designated or constituted. \n \n\"RFP\" means the Request for Proposals issued by the VAA on the 13th day of February 2025 entitled, 2025 \nParking Management Services, which RFP is attached to this Contract as Appendix ‘B’ to Schedule B. \n \n“Sales Taxes” means the sales taxes at the retailer level, the amount of which is determined by the amount of \nsales made and which is required to be collected and account for to any provincial or federal authority.   \n \n\"Scope of Work\" means the Work described in Schedule 'B' of the Contract and the Contract Documents. \n \n“Shared Use Curb” means the shared lane in front of the YYJ terminal primarily used to pick up and drop off \ntravelers via privately owned vehicles plus taxis, Uber, and similar.  \n \n\"Short Term Parking Lot\" means the parking lot as more particularly shown on the drawing attached to the RFP \nas Appendix A – YYJ PARKING FACILITIES. \n \n\"Subcontractor\" means a person, firm or corporation having a direct contract with the Contractor to perform a \npart or parts of the Work. \n \n\"Term\" has the meaning ascribed to it in Part 5 of the Articles of Agreement and includes any renewal or extension \nthereof. \n \n\"Understated Gross Revenue\" means any Gross Revenue that has been understated, by the Contractor, on the \nMonthly Statement of Account or Annual Gross Revenue Statement submitted by the Contractor to the VAA. \n \n\"VAA\" means the Victoria Airport Authority and includes any of its successors or assigns; in any section of this \nContract that contains a release, hold harmless, indemnity or other exculpatory language in favour of the VAA the \nterm \"VAA \" also means any directors, officers, servants, employees, agents or contractors of the VAA and any \nother Person for whom the VAA may be responsible for in law. \n \n\"Work\" means the services provided by the Contractor to the VAA with respect to the Contractor's management, \nadministration and maintenance of parking at, upon and within the Parking Facilities pursuant to the Contract \nDocuments including the VAA’s Request for Proposal and the Contractor’s Proposal. \n  \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "RFP Issue Date", :date "2025-02-13", :time nil, :timezone nil, :evidence "RFP issued by the VAA on the 13th day of February 2025"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority issuing the RFP", :contact nil, :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Victoria Airport Authority and its successors, assigns, directors, officers, servants, employees, agents or contractors", :contact nil, :evidence "\"VAA\" means the Victoria Airport Authority"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Entity providing management, administration and maintenance of parking", :contact nil, :evidence "services provided by the Contractor to the VAA with respect to the Contractor's management, administration and maintenance of parking"} {:name "Subcontractor", :role "Person, firm or corporation having a direct contract with the Contractor", :contact nil, :evidence "\"Subcontractor\" means a person, firm or corporation having a direct contract with the Contractor"} {:name "Uber", :role "Transportation service provider using the Shared Use Curb", :contact nil, :evidence "primarily used to pick up and drop off travelers via privately owned vehicles plus taxis, Uber, and similar"}], :financials [{:item "Sales Taxes", :amount_or_terms "Determined by the amount of sales made; required to be collected and accounted for to provincial or federal authority", :evidence "“Sales Taxes” means the sales taxes at the retailer level, the amount of which is determined by the amount of sales made and which is required to be collected and account for to any provincial or federal authority."} {:item "Understated Gross Revenue", :amount_or_terms "Gross Revenue understated on the Monthly Statement of Account or Annual Gross Revenue Statement", :evidence "\"Understated Gross Revenue\" means any Gross Revenue that has been understated, by the Contractor, on the Monthly Statement of Account or Annual Gross Revenue Statement"}], :summary_points ["Defines 'Parking Transactions' based on the activation of entrance gates at the Short Term Lot and exit gates at the Daily Parking Lot." "Establishes legal definitions for entities involved, including the VAA, Contractors, Subcontractors, and the broader definition of a 'Person'." "Specifies requirements for financial reporting, including Sales Taxes and the identification of Understated Gross Revenue in monthly or annual statements." "Describes the 'Shared Use Curb' as the lane for traveler pick-up and drop-off by private vehicles, taxis, and ride-sharing services like Uber."]}} {:page-number 79, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 79\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 10 of 67 \n \nSCHEDULE 'B' \nSCOPE OF WORK \n \nTABLE OF CONTENTS \n \nPART 1  GENERAL          11 \n1.1  Management Services         11 \n1.2  Contractual Adjustment for Employee Parking Lot      12 \n1.3  Modification of Parking Facilities        13 \n1.4  Operational Review         14 \n1.5  Property Taxes          14 \n \nPART 2  CONDUCT OF WORK         14 \n2.1  Marketing          14 \n2.2  American Currency         14 \n2.3  Collection of Parking Fees        14 \n2.4  Credit Cards          15  \n2.5  Contractor's Parking         15 \n2.6  Hours of Operation         15 \n2.7  Operational Reports & Related Requirements      16 \n2.8  Parking Enforcement         16 \n2.9  Parking Fees          17 \n2.10  Personnel          17 \n2.11  Response to Customer Complaints       18 \n2.12  Towing           18 \n2.13  Training           19 \n \nPART 3  FINANCIAL REQUIREMENTS        19 \n3.1  Collection of Monies and Related Reports       19 \n3.2  Financial Controls and Internal Audit Procedures      20 \n3.3  Financial Loss          20 \n3.4  Inspection and Audit         20 \n \nPART 4  PARKING BUILDINGS, EQUIPMENT & FACILITIES      22  \n4.1  Buildings          22 \n4.2  Parking Equipment         22 \n4.3  Parking Facilities          22 \n \nAPPENDICES \nAppendix 'A' Parking Facilities – Maintenance & Repair Responsibilities     25 \nAppendix ‘B’ VAA’s Request for Proposals        26 \nAppendix ‘C’ Contractor’s Proposal         27 \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Issuing Authority", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "Contractor's Parking; Contractor’s Proposal"}], :financials [{:item "Property Taxes", :amount_or_terms "To be defined in section 1.5", :evidence "1.5  Property Taxes"} {:item "Collection of Parking Fees", :amount_or_terms "To be defined in section 2.3", :evidence "2.3  Collection of Parking Fees"} {:item "Parking Fees", :amount_or_terms "To be defined in section 2.9", :evidence "2.9  Parking Fees"} {:item "Financial Loss", :amount_or_terms "To be defined in section 3.3", :evidence "3.3  Financial Loss"}], :summary_points ["This page serves as the Table of Contents for Schedule 'B' (Scope of Work) of the 2025 Parking Management Services RFP." "The scope covers general management services, conduct of work including marketing and enforcement, and specific financial requirements/controls." "Financial sections include provisions for property taxes, collection of fees, American currency handling, and internal audit procedures." "Appendices are listed covering maintenance responsibilities, the original RFP, and the contractor's proposal."]}} {:page-number 80, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 80\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 11 of 67 \n \nPART 1 GENERAL \n \n1.1 MANAGEMENT SERVICES  \n \n1.1.1 The Contractor will throughout the Term of this Contract, supply to the satisfaction of the VAA as and when \nrequired by the VAA, all Work required of the Contractor in accordance with this Contract, including, \nwithout limitation: \n \na) Day-to-Day Operations - Manage the day-to-day operation of the YYJ Parking Facilities and shared \nuse of terminal curb, including establishing operational plans, collecting revenue, monitoring parking \nand pick-up / drop-off activity, and maximizing utilization of the lots to ensure that parking availability \nis optimized for the traveling public, all while maintaining a First-Class level of responsiveness, \nprofessionalism and operational capability.  \n \nb) Monitor Equipment Issues - Monitor and report issues related to the Parking Equipment located in \nthe Parking Facilities. The Contractor may be asked to assist with troubleshooting, but will not be \nrequired to provide maintenance and repairs; \n \nc) Supplies and Consumables - Provide all consumables (i.e., stationery, control forms, customer \nsatisfaction/incident reports and cleaning supplies), and any equipment other than the Parking \nEquipment that may be required for the day-to-day operation, management and maintenance of the \nParking Facilities. Spare parts are provided by Precise Parklink and covered under the extended \nwarranty and maintenance agreement. Entry tickets and receipts will be monitored by the Contractor \nand ordered through Precise Parklink as required;   \n \nd) Air Terminal Employee and Commuter (Airline Pilots & Flight Attendants) Parking Permit \nManagement – Contractor will manage the process for issuing and retrieving air terminal employee \nand commuter parking permits, including invoicing, billing and collection.  \n \ne) Monthly Public Parking – Contractor will manage monthly public parking program, including billing \nand collection.  \n \nf) Lot Attendant - Provide a lot attendant to assist customers with Parking Equipment and assisting with \nParking Equipment breakdown and traffic direction. This individual also handles in-person cashiering \ntransactions and other customer interactions, including but not limited to dispute resolution; \n \ng) Onsite Inspections - Inspect the Parking Facilities, including the Parking Equipment, buildings and \nbooths therein, and notify the VAA of any deficiencies including ordinary wear and tear requiring \nremedy by the VAA in accordance with this Contract; \n \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Owner/Issuing Authority", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Owner/Issuing Authority", :evidence "supply to the satisfaction of the VAA as and when required by the VAA"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "The Contractor will throughout the Term of this Contract, supply to the satisfaction of the VAA... all Work required"} {:name "Precise Parklink", :role "Equipment and Maintenance provider", :evidence "Spare parts are provided by Precise Parklink and covered under the extended warranty and maintenance agreement."}], :financials [{:item "Revenue Collection", :amount_or_terms "Contractor responsible for collecting revenue", :evidence "collecting revenue, monitoring parking and pick-up / drop-off activity"} {:item "Permit Billing and Collection", :amount_or_terms "Contractor managed process including invoicing, billing and collection", :evidence "Contractor will manage the process for issuing and retrieving air terminal employee and commuter parking permits, including invoicing, billing and collection."} {:item "Monthly Public Parking Management", :amount_or_terms "Contractor managed process including billing and collection", :evidence "Contractor will manage monthly public parking program, including billing and collection."} {:item "Parking Equipment Maintenance and Parts", :amount_or_terms "Covered under extended warranty and maintenance agreement via Precise Parklink", :evidence "Spare parts are provided by Precise Parklink and covered under the extended warranty and maintenance agreement."}], :summary_points ["The Contractor is responsible for the day-to-day management of YYJ Parking Facilities, including revenue collection and optimizing lot utilization." "Operational duties include managing parking permits for employees and commuters, as well as the monthly public parking program." "While the Contractor monitors equipment and assists with troubleshooting, maintenance and spare parts are provided by Precise Parklink under a separate agreement." "The Contractor must provide on-site lot attendants for customer assistance, traffic direction, and manual cashiering transactions."]}} {:page-number 81, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 81\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 12 of 67 \n \nh) Facilities Maintenance - Maintain the Parking Facilities in a clean and neat condition at all times \nincluding daily litter pickup; \n \ni) Parking Enforcement - Subject to the approval of the VAA, establish and enforce policies for parking \nviolations which may include violation notices, penalties and towing; \n \nj) Curb Management Program – Create and administer the approved Curb Management Program, \nproviding staffing at and oversight of the shared pick-up / drop-off Airport Terminal curb to manage \ncurb activity;  \n \nk) Revenue Controls - Establish and operate processes and controls relative to collection, \ndocumentation, and reporting of cash payments only; \n \nl) Monthly Statement – In accordance with Subsection 1.3.2 of Schedule C of this Contract – PAYMENT \nTERMS, prepare and submit to the VAA, a Monthly Statement of Account in a form satisfactory to \nthe VAA relative to all Gross Revenue generated by the Contractor's management and operation of \nthe Parking Facilities and the Contractor's Management Fee; and \n \nm) Snow and Ice Removal - Maintaining the Parking Facilities for snow removal and ice control, based \non the Snow and Ice Removal Map attached to the RFP as Appendix C – ICE CONTROL AND SNOW \nREMOVAL MAP.  \n \n1.1.2 The Contractor will maintain, as and when required by the VAA and to the satisfaction of the VAA, adequate \ncommunications equipment such that the VAA is able to contact supervisory personnel twenty-four (24) \nhours a day, seven (7) days a week, and supervisory personnel will be available to attend the Airport for all \nemergency conditions. \n \n1.1.3 The Contractor will maintain head office support between the hours of 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Pacific Time \nZone, Monday to Friday, at a minimum to resolve customer service complaints, monitor operations and \nprovide a communications link with the VAA. \n \n1.2 CONTRACTUAL ADJUSTMENT FOR EMPLOYEE PARKING LOT  \n \n1.2.1 The VAA reserves the right in its sole discretion to delete from this Contract the Contractor's management \nof the Employee Parking Lot. \n \n1.2.2 The VAA will give the Contractor no fewer than thirty (30) Days prior written notice of the effective date of \nany such deletion. From and after the effective date of a change aforesaid, the terms and conditions of this \nContract will no longer have application to the Employee Parking Lot so deleted from the Parking Facilities, \nas the case may be, without further amendment to this Contract. A copy of the written notice will be \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Head office support hours", :time "08:00-17:00", :timezone "Pacific Time Zone", :evidence "head office support between the hours of 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Pacific Time Zone, Monday to Friday"} {:name "Notice period for deletion of Employee Parking Lot", :date nil, :time nil, :evidence "no fewer than thirty (30) Days prior written notice"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Issuing Authority", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Contract Administrator", :evidence "Subject to the approval of the VAA, establish and enforce policies"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider / Manager", :evidence "Contractor's management and operation of the Parking Facilities"}], :financials [{:item "Monthly Statement of Account", :amount_or_terms "Reporting of Gross Revenue and Management Fee in accordance with Subsection 1.3.2 of Schedule C", :evidence "prepare and submit to the VAA, a Monthly Statement of Account in a form satisfactory to the VAA relative to all Gross Revenue generated by the Contractor's management and operation of the Parking Facilities and the Contractor's Management Fee"} {:item "Parking Violations", :amount_or_terms "May include violation notices and penalties", :evidence "enforce policies for parking violations which may include violation notices, penalties and towing"}], :summary_points ["The Contractor is responsible for site maintenance, curb management, parking enforcement, and snow/ice removal." "Operational requirements include 24/7 availability for emergency supervisory contact and weekday head office support during business hours." "Financial reporting requires a Monthly Statement of Account covering gross revenues and management fees." "The Victoria Airport Authority reserves the right to remove the Employee Parking Lot from the contract with 30 days' notice."]}} {:page-number 82, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 82\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 13 of 67 \n \nattached to and form part of this Contract. \n \n1.2.3 If in the opinion of either the VAA or the Contractor acting reasonably any such deletion or addition \npursuant to Clause 1.2.1 and 1.2.2 necessitates an adjustment to the Management Fee then in effect, that \nparty will provide the other party with details of the proposed adjustment to the Management Fee for that \nparty's approval no less than thirty (30) Days prior to the effective date of the change stipulated by the VAA.  \nIf the Contractor and the VAA are not able to agree on whether or not an adjustment to the Management \nFee is necessary or appropriate, the parties will resolve the dispute pursuant to the provisions of Part 5 of \nSchedule 'E' - DISPUTES. The Management Fee in effect prior to the date of the effective change aforesaid \nwill continue in effect until such time as the disagreement between the Contractor and the VAA has been \nresolved, such resolution being retroactive to the initial deletion of the Employee Parking Lot from the \nParking Facilities. \n \n1.3 MODIFICATION OF PARKING FACILITIES \n \n1.3.1 The VAA may at any time and from time to time during the Term of this Contract in its sole discretion: \n \na) add parking spaces to or delete parking spaces from the Parking Facilities; \n \nb) add designated areas to or delete designated areas from the Parking Facilities; or \n \nc) make changes to the Parking Equipment, by removing, replacing, altering, or adding to the existing \nParking Equipment in the Parking Facilities. \n \n1.3.2 The VAA will give the Contractor no fewer than thirty (30) Days prior written notice of the effective date of \nany such addition or deletion. From and after the effective date of a change aforesaid, the terms and \nconditions of this Contract will no longer have application to any such parking spaces, designated areas, or \nParking Equipment so deleted from the Parking Facilities and will extend to such additional parking spaces, \ndesignated areas, or Parking Equipment, as the case may be, without further amendment to this Contract. \nA copy of the written notice will be attached to and form part of this Contract. \n \n1.3.3 If in the opinion of either the VAA or the Contractor acting reasonably any such additions to or deletions \nfrom the Parking Facilities pursuant to Clause 1.3.1 and 1.3.2 above necessitate an adjustment to the \nManagement Fee then in effect that party will provide the other party with details of the proposed \nadjustment to the Management Fee for that party's approval no less than thirty (30) Days prior to the \neffective date of the change stipulated by the VAA.   If the Contractor and the VAA are not able to agree on \nwhether or not an adjustment to the Management Fee is necessary or appropriate, the parties will resolve \nthe dispute pursuant to the provisions of Part 5 of Schedule 'E' - DISPUTES.  The Management Fee in effect \nprior to the date of effective change aforesaid will continue in effect until such time as the disagreement \nbetween the Contractor and the VAA has been resolved, such resolution being retroactive to the initial \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Notice period for adjustment to Management Fee", :evidence "no less than thirty (30) Days prior to the effective date of the change stipulated by the VAA."} {:name "Notice period for modification of Parking Facilities", :evidence "VAA will give the Contractor no fewer than thirty (30) Days prior written notice of the effective date of any such addition or deletion."}], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Authority (VAA)", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "If in the opinion of either the VAA or the Contractor acting reasonably"}], :financials [{:item "Management Fee", :amount_or_terms "Subject to adjustment based on deletions or additions to parking facilities/equipment; requires 30 days notice for proposed adjustment.", :evidence "necessitates an adjustment to the Management Fee then in effect, that party will provide the other party with details of the proposed adjustment to the Management Fee for that party's approval no less than thirty (30) Days prior to the effective date"} {:item "Management Fee during disputes", :amount_or_terms "Fee in effect prior to change continues until resolution; resolution is retroactive.", :evidence "The Management Fee in effect prior to the date of the effective change aforesaid will continue in effect until such time as the disagreement between the Contractor and the VAA has been resolved, such resolution being retroactive"}], :summary_points ["The Victoria Airport Authority (VAA) reserves the right to modify parking facilities by adding or removing spaces, designated areas, or parking equipment at its discretion." "Modifications to facilities require the VAA to provide at least 30 days' written notice to the Contractor." "Either party may propose an adjustment to the Management Fee due to facility changes, provided notice is given 30 days before the effective change date." "Disputes regarding Management Fee adjustments are resolved via Schedule 'E', with existing fees remaining in place until a retroactive resolution is reached."]}} {:page-number 83, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 83\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 14 of 67 \n \naddition or deletion of parking spaces, designated areas, or parking equipment in the Parking Facilities. \n \n1.4 OPERATIONAL REVIEW \n1.4.1 Unless outlined otherwise in this Contract, the Contractor agrees that during the Term of this Contract, it \nshall adhere to and perform each and every one of the undertakings and representations outlined in the \nContractor’s Proposal, as well as any subsequent representations made by the Contractor to the VAA.  The \nContractor further covenants and agrees that any failure to comply with the above requirement shall \nconstitute a material breach of the conditions of the Contract for the purpose of Part 4 of Schedule 'E' - \nNON-COMPLIANCE, SUSPENSION AND TERMINATION. \n \n1.5 PROPERTY TAXES \n \n1.5.1 The VAA will be responsible for payment of all municipal property taxes. \n \n \nPART 2 CONDUCT OF WORK \n \n2.1 MARKETING  \n \nThe successful Proponent will implement a robust marketing plan to optimize parking revenue, utilization, \nand customer service.  The marketing initiatives could include internet-based parking marketing \ntechniques, including pre-paid reservations. All marketing must be in both official languages (English and \nFrench) and be pre-approved by the Authority. It is expected that the Proponent would budget 0.5% of \npublic parking Revenues toward Marketing. \n \n2.2 AMERICAN CURRENCY \n \n2.2.1 The Contractor will accept US currency in payment for parking and the parties agree that the exchange rate \ngranted will not differ by more than two (2) percentage points from the \"buy\" rate set by the Royal Bank of \nCanada, from time to time. The Contractor will inform the public of the exchange rate granted by displaying \nsigns indicating the exchange rate in locations determined by the VAA. \n \n2.3 COLLECTION OF PARKING FEES \n \n2.3.1 The Contractor will collect Parking Fees from all users of the Parking Facilities, unless waived by the VAA. \n \n2.3.2 The VAA hereby waives Parking Fees for Members of Parliament (MP's) using the Parking Facilities. \n \n2.3.3 The Contractor will make every reasonable effort to collect unpaid Parking Fees. At a minimum, reasonable \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / Contracting Entity", :contact nil, :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Authority / Contracting Entity", :contact nil, :evidence "representations made by the Contractor to the VAA"} {:name "Royal Bank of Canada", :role "Financial Institution (Exchange Rate Reference)", :contact nil, :evidence "\"buy\" rate set by the Royal Bank of Canada"} {:name "Members of Parliament (MP's)", :role "Users exempt from parking fees", :contact nil, :evidence "The VAA hereby waives Parking Fees for Members of Parliament (MP's)"}], :financials [{:item "Municipal property taxes", :amount_or_terms "VAA will be responsible for payment", :evidence "The VAA will be responsible for payment of all municipal property taxes."} {:item "Marketing Budget", :amount_or_terms "0.5% of public parking Revenues", :evidence "It is expected that the Proponent would budget 0.5% of public parking Revenues toward Marketing."} {:item "US Currency Exchange Rate", :amount_or_terms "Not more than two (2) percentage points difference from Royal Bank of Canada \"buy\" rate", :evidence "exchange rate granted will not differ by more than two (2) percentage points from the \"buy\" rate set by the Royal Bank of Canada"} {:item "Parking Fee Waiver", :amount_or_terms "Waived for Members of Parliament (MP's)", :evidence "The VAA hereby waives Parking Fees for Members of Parliament (MP's) using the Parking Facilities."}], :summary_points ["The Contractor is bound to all representations made in their proposal; failure to comply constitutes a material breach." "Successful proponents must implement a bilingual (English/French) marketing plan and budget 0.5% of parking revenues for marketing activities." "Victoria Airport Authority (VAA) remains responsible for municipal property taxes." "The Contractor must accept US currency at an exchange rate closely tied to the Royal Bank of Canada's buy rate and must post these rates publicly."]}} {:page-number 84, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 84\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 15 of 67 \n \neffort will include an initial collection letter to the delinquent vehicle owner within thirty (30) Days of \nParking Fees being unpaid, and a second letter in cases where Parking Fees remain unpaid after thirty (30) \nDays from the date of the initial letter. As a third step, unpaid tickets should be forwarded to the collections \nbranch for recovery, after thirty (30) days of the issuance of the second letter. \n \n2.3.4 Any failure by the Contractor to demonstrate reasonable effort in the collection of any unpaid Parking Fee \nwill result in the Contractor assuming payment responsibility for that unpaid Parking Fee. \n \n2.3.5 Payment of Parking Fees received through the mail are to be recorded on the Monthly Statement of \nAccount submitted to the VAA. \n \n2.4 CREDIT CARDS \n \n2.4.1 The Contractor will accept all major credit cards as payment for parking in the Parking Facilities. \n \n2.5 CONTRACTOR'S PARKING \n \n2.5.1 The Contractor and its employees may park in the Parking Facilities as designated by the VAA from time to \ntime, and such employees may park free of charge for the period of time only that they are actively on shift \nand performing their duties. Under no other circumstances may the Contractor’s employees use the Parking \nFacilities for personal parking. \n \n2.6 HOURS OF OPERATION \n \n2.6.1 Parking Facilities are available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.  The parking exit booth for Lot 1 (green lot) \nwill be staffed by the Contractor for a minimum of 20 hours a day. The Contractor will provide continuous \nservice to the travelling public by staffing the Parking Facilities on a full-time basis, with Contractor’s hours \nof operations sufficient to provide service for all arriving and departing flights, with hours subject to \nincrease or decrease based on incoming or outgoing flight schedules. Posted hours of operations may \nchange on occasion as approved by the VAA. The parking exit booth for Long-Term Lot 2 may require \nstaffing during peak holiday periods such as Thanksgiving and Christmas, at the direction of the VAA.  \n \n2.6.2 The Contractor will extend the hours of operation beyond those set out in Clause 2.6.1, as and when \nrequired by the VAA, to cover late or early flight arrivals and departures.    \n \n2.6.3 At the commencement of the Term of this Contract, the Contractor will provide the following staffing levels: \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Initial collection letter deadline", :evidence "initial collection letter to the delinquent vehicle owner within thirty (30) Days of Parking Fees being unpaid"} {:name "Second collection letter deadline", :evidence "second letter in cases where Parking Fees remain unpaid after thirty (30) Days from the date of the initial letter"} {:name "Collections branch forwarding deadline", :evidence "unpaid tickets should be forwarded to the collections branch for recovery, after thirty (30) days of the issuance of the second letter"} {:name "Peak staffing period: Thanksgiving", :evidence "staffing during peak holiday periods such as Thanksgiving"} {:name "Peak staffing period: Christmas", :evidence "staffing during peak holiday periods such as ... Christmas"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / Issuer", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Authority", :evidence "submitted to the VAA."} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "The Contractor will accept all major credit cards"} {:name "Collections branch", :role "Debt recovery", :evidence "forwarded to the collections branch for recovery"}], :financials [{:item "Unpaid Parking Fee Responsibility", :amount_or_terms "Contractor assuming payment responsibility if reasonable collection effort is not demonstrated", :evidence "Any failure by the Contractor to demonstrate reasonable effort in the collection of any unpaid Parking Fee will result in the Contractor assuming payment responsibility for that unpaid Parking Fee."} {:item "Parking Fees via Mail", :amount_or_terms "Recorded on Monthly Statement of Account", :evidence "Payment of Parking Fees received through the mail are to be recorded on the Monthly Statement of Account submitted to the VAA."} {:item "Credit Card Acceptance", :amount_or_terms "Accept all major credit cards", :evidence "The Contractor will accept all major credit cards as payment for parking"} {:item "Contractor Employee Parking", :amount_or_terms "Free of charge (only while on shift)", :evidence "such employees may park free of charge for the period of time only that they are actively on shift and performing their duties."}], :summary_points ["Establishes a three-stage debt collection process for unpaid parking fees occurring in 30-day increments." "Requires the Contractor to staff the Lot 1 exit booth for a minimum of 20 hours per day and maintain overall hours sufficient to cover all flight schedules." "Mandates that the Contractor assume financial liability for unpaid fees if they fail to demonstrate 'reasonable effort' in collection tasks." "Specifies that employee parking is only free during active work shifts and prohibits personal use of parking facilities."]}} {:page-number 85, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 85\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 16 of 67 \n \n \nPosition Coverage in Hours per Day \nOn-Site Manager 8 \nLot Attendants Minimum 20 \nCurb Management Officer Minimum 15.5 \n \n2.6.4 The VAA reserves the right to require the Contractor to effect changes in the shift schedules to meet \noperational needs. \n \n2.7 OPERATIONAL REPORTS & RELATED REQUIREMENTS \n \n2.7.1 The Contractor will be responsible for producing the following operational reports and providing the same \nto the VAA as scheduled and when requested: \n \nReport Frequency  \nEmployee Shift Schedules and Hours of Work \n(including timesheets) \nAs requested by VAA \nList of current employees Monthly and as requested by VAA \n# of Revenue Parking Transactions by Parking Lot Weekly and as requested by VAA \n# of Non-Revenue Parking Transactions by Parking \nLot \nWeekly and as requested by VAA \nAbandoned Vehicle Report  As requested by VAA \nCustomer Complaint Report  As requested by VAA \nIncident Report As requested by VAA \nSnow Removal and Ice Control Report As requested by VAA \nEmployee Parking As requested by VAA \nCommuter Parking As requested by VAA \nPublic Monthly Parking As requested by VAA \nAd hoc Reports as Requested by VAA As requested by VAA \n \n2.8 PARKING ENFORCEMENT \n \n2.8.1 In the event the VAA, after consultation with the Contractor, establishes a reasonable enforcement \npolicy for vehicles parked without permission in the Short-Term Parking Lot, the Employee Parking Lot, \nand the Commercial Vehicle Lane the Contractor will implement the enforcement policy. \n \nThe Contractor further acknowledges and agrees that any and all revenue generated from violation \npolicies and penalties will constitute part of the Gross Revenue under this Contract.  Notwithstanding \nconsultation by the VAA with the Contractor, the Contractor will implement the enforcement policy as \nand when determined by the VAA. \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Issuing Authority (VAA)", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "On-Site Manager", :role "Staffing Position", :evidence "On-Site Manager 8"} {:name "Lot Attendants", :role "Staffing Position", :evidence "Lot Attendants Minimum 20"} {:name "Curb Management Officer", :role "Staffing Position", :evidence "Curb Management Officer Minimum 15.5"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "The VAA reserves the right to require the Contractor to effect changes in the shift schedules"}], :financials [{:item "Revenue from violation policies and penalties", :amount_or_terms "Constitutes part of the Gross Revenue under this Contract", :evidence "The Contractor further acknowledges and agrees that any and all revenue generated from violation policies and penalties will constitute part of the Gross Revenue under this Contract."}], :summary_points ["Defines minimum daily staffing coverage hours for the On-Site Manager (8), Lot Attendants (20), and Curb Management Officer (15.5)." "Outlines mandatory operational reports including weekly parking transaction data and monthly employee lists." "Grants Victoria Airport Authority the right to adjust shift schedules and establish enforcement policies for unauthorized parking." "Specifies that all revenue generated from parking violations and penalties must be included in the project's Gross Revenue."]}} {:page-number 86, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 86\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 17 of 67 \n \n \n2.9 PARKING FEES \n \n2.9.1 The VAA is solely responsible for setting the Parking Fees for the Parking Facilities. \n \n2.9.2 The Parking Fees at the commencement of the Term of this Contract are as set out in Appendix 'B' to \nthe RFP – PARKING LOT RATES. The VAA may make amendments thereto from time to time during the \ncurrency of this Contract and the Contractor agrees that the VAA may advise the Contractor of the \nrevised Parking Fees by forwarding to the Contractor a written notice of such changes.  Upon receipt by \nthe Contractor of such notice from the VAA, the Contractor will, as and when determined by the VAA, \nimplement the revised Parking Fees including any updates to the Parking Equipment and other necessary \ncomputer updates that may be required for acceptance and collection of the revised Parking Fees \nwithout further amendment to this Contract.  Such revised Parking Fees will supersede all previous \nParking Fees, and a copy of the written notice will be attached to and form part of this Contract. \n \n2.10 PERSONNEL \n \n2.10.1 The Contractor will maintain a local office presence for the duration of the Term, either currently \nestablished or to be established within one (1) month of Contract commencement.  \n \n2.10.2 The Contractor will maintain an on-site manager. \n \n2.10.3 The Contractor will be responsible for the hiring, dismissal, discipline, training, direction and control of \nall personnel required to perform the Work under this Contract.  \n \n2.10.4 The Contractor warrants that all Persons (including all Subcontractors and suppliers) employed or \nretained by the Contractor to perform the Work or any part of the Work are fully competent and capable \nof doing the Work. \n \n2.10.5 The Contractor is required to pay all personnel a competitive hourly rate of pay, exclusive of benefits. \nBenefits provided must also be competitive as compared to the applicable market.  \n \n2.10.6 The Contractor will ensure that all its personnel are properly groomed and will be required to supply all \npersonnel with uniforms that are approved by the VAA.  \n \n2.10.7 The Contractor and its employees, agents and contractors shall comply with all reasonable rules and \noperating procedures relative to the management of the Airport, including without limitation, those \nrelating to service, safety, security and matters of urgency. \n \n2.10.8 The Contractor will ensure that all its personnel are polite and courteous at all times to passengers, other \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Local office establishment deadline", :date nil, :time nil, :timezone nil, :evidence "within one (1) month of Contract commencement"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Owner/Authority responsible for setting Parking Fees and approving uniforms", :contact nil, :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY; The VAA is solely responsible for setting the Parking Fees"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service provider responsible for parking management, equipment updates, and personnel management", :contact nil, :evidence "The Contractor will maintain a local office presence"} {:name "On-site manager", :role "Management personnel maintained by Contractor", :contact nil, :evidence "The Contractor will maintain an on-site manager."} {:name "Subcontractors and suppliers", :role "Entities employed or retained by the Contractor", :contact nil, :evidence "including all Subcontractors and suppliers"}], :financials [{:item "Parking Fees", :amount_or_terms "As set out in Appendix 'B' – PARKING LOT RATES; subject to amendment by VAA", :evidence "The Parking Fees at the commencement of the Term of this Contract are as set out in Appendix 'B' to the RFP – PARKING LOT RATES."} {:item "Personnel Pay", :amount_or_terms "Competitive hourly rate of pay, exclusive of benefits", :evidence "The Contractor is required to pay all personnel a competitive hourly rate of pay, exclusive of benefits."} {:item "Personnel Benefits", :amount_or_terms "Competitive as compared to the applicable market", :evidence "Benefits provided must also be competitive as compared to the applicable market."}], :summary_points ["The Victoria Airport Authority (VAA) retains sole authority over setting and amending parking fees, which the Contractor must implement in equipment and computer systems upon notice." "The Contractor is required to maintain a local office within one month of contract commencement and provide an on-site manager." "The Contractor is responsible for all personnel management, including hiring, training, and supplying VAA-approved uniforms." "Contractor staff must be paid competitive market wages and benefits, and are required to adhere to all airport safety, security, and conduct procedures."]}} {:page-number 87, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 87\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 18 of 67 \n \nmembers of the public, and Airport employees. The Contractor will, upon the request of the VAA, \nremove any personnel who, in the opinion of the VAA, is incompetent or has acted improperly, and the \nContractor will not permit a person who has been removed to return to the work site unless the prior \nwritten consent of the VAA has been obtained. \n \n2.10.9 If the VAA determines that national security is involved, it may instruct the Contractor to provide \ninformation concerning any Person or Persons employed by the Contractor on the Airport and may \nrequire the removal of any such Person or Persons from the Airport if determined to be necessary for \nnational security.  The Contractor shall comply with instructions from the VAA pursuant to this Section \n2.10. \n \n2.10.10 The Contractor will, as and when required by the VAA and to the satisfaction of the VAA, prepare and \nmaintain an operations and procedures manual for the Parking Facilities and will ensure that all \npersonnel have knowledge of its contents. \n \n2.11 RESPONSE TO CUSTOMER COMPLAINTS \n \n2.11.1 The Contractor will develop and maintain a written process for resolving customer complaints, within \nthirty (30) days of commencement of this Agreement.  \n \n2.11.2 The Contractor will log all customer complaints and provide a Customer Complaint Report to the VAA \nupon request. \n \n2.11.3 The Contractor will have a manager or supervisor available on-site or by telephone that can \ncommunicate directly with on-site personnel to immediately respond and, if necessary, attend the \nAirport to address customer service issues. \n \n2.12 TOWING \n \n2.12.1 In the event the VAA, after consultation with the Contractor, establishes a reasonable towing policy for \nvehicles parked without permission in the Parking Facilities, the Contractor will implement the towing \npolicy and the Contractor, or a party authorized by it, will do the towing necessary to adhere to the \ntowing policy of the VAA. The Contractor will indemnify and save harmless the VAA from all costs, \nexpenses, damages, suits or causes of action paid, incurred or suffered by the VAA as a result of the \ntowing of a vehicle in a manner contrary or inconsistent with the towing policy or resulting from \nnegligence in towing of a vehicle. Notwithstanding consultation by the VAA with the Contractor, the \nContractor will implement the towing policy as and when determined by the VAA. \n \n \n \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Development of written process for customer complaints", :date nil, :time nil, :timezone nil, :evidence "within thirty (30) days of commencement of this Agreement"}], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Authority / Requesting Entity", :contact nil, :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :contact nil, :evidence "The Contractor will, upon the request of the VAA, remove any personnel"} {:name "VAA", :role "Abbreviation for Victoria Airport Authority", :contact nil, :evidence "upon the request of the VAA"} {:name "Airport employees", :role "Personnel", :contact nil, :evidence "members of the public, and Airport employees"} {:name "manager or supervisor", :role "Contractor staff for customer service response", :contact nil, :evidence "The Contractor will have a manager or supervisor available on-site or by telephone"}], :financials [{:item "Indemnification for towing", :amount_or_terms "Contractor will indemnify and save harmless the VAA from all costs, expenses, damages, suits or causes of action resulting from towing inconsistencies or negligence.", :evidence "The Contractor will indemnify and save harmless the VAA from all costs, expenses, damages, suits or causes of action paid, incurred or suffered by the VAA as a result of the towing of a vehicle in a manner contrary or inconsistent with the towing policy or resulting from negligence"}], :summary_points ["The Victoria Airport Authority (VAA) reserves the right to demand the removal of any contractor personnel for incompetence, improper conduct, or national security reasons." "The Contractor is required to maintain an operations and procedures manual and develop a customer complaint resolution process within 30 days of contract commencement." "A manager or supervisor must be available at all times (on-site or via telephone) to handle customer service issues and attend the airport if necessary." "The Contractor is responsible for implementing the VAA's towing policy and assumes full liability/indemnity for damages or legal actions resulting from towing operations."]}} {:page-number 88, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 88\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 19 of 67 \n \n2.13 TRAINING  \n \n2.13.1 The Contractor will train all personnel as required to perform the Work under this Contract.  Such \ntraining will be provided at the Contractor's expense and records may be requested by the VAA in \npreparation for periodic audits conducted by the Canadian Transportation Agency (CTA).  Training will \ninclude as a minimum: \n \na) customer service training program (WorldHost Customer Service training or the equivalent); \nb) A minimum of 12 hours of ‘on the job' training prior to placing personnel on their own in the \nfield; and \nc) technical training on the operation of all Parking Equipment operation, including without \nlimitation computer systems, software, changing paper rolls and print cartridges, restocking \nticket machines, and CCTV operation. \n \n2.13.2 The Contractor will provide all personnel who may interact with the travelling public at the Airport with \nSensitivity Training (WorldHost – Inclusive Service or the equivalent) at the level required to ensure that \nits personnel possess the knowledge, skills and attitudes necessary to assist persons with disabilities in \nan effective and sensitive manner. All such training will comply with the Personnel Training Regulations \nfor the Assistance of Persons with Disabilities (the \"Regulations\").  The Contractor will ensure that all \npersonnel will complete their initial training within sixty (60) Days after the commencement of their \nduties as well as receive periodic refresher training sessions appropriate to the requirements of their \nfunction. The Contractor will keep its training program current and available for inspection by the \nCanadian Transportation Agency, the VAA and the general public. \n \n2.13.3  All employees of the Contractor must be trained for (by VAA), possess and carry valid Landside ID (“LID”) \ncredential while working at YYJ.  \n \n2.13.4 Additional VAA-required and administered training includes:  \n• Accessibility Training \n• Sunflower Program (hidden disabilities) \n• And other future training programs as required by VAA. \n \n \nPART 3 FINANCIAL REQUIREMENTS \n \n3.1 COLLECTION OF MONIES & RELATED REPORTS \n \n3.1.1 All Monies collected will be the exclusive property of the VAA and will be held in trust by the Contractor for \nthe VAA. \n \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Initial Training Deadline", :date nil, :time nil, :timezone nil, :evidence "The Contractor will ensure that all personnel will complete their initial training within sixty (60) Days after the commencement of their duties"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / Owner", :contact nil, :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service provider responsible for personnel training and revenue collection", :contact nil, :evidence "The Contractor will train all personnel as required to perform the Work under this Contract."} {:name "Canadian Transportation Agency (CTA)", :role "Regulatory body conducting audits", :contact nil, :evidence "periodic audits conducted by the Canadian Transportation Agency (CTA)"} {:name "VAA", :role "Acronym for Victoria Airport Authority", :contact nil, :evidence "records may be requested by the VAA"} {:name "YYJ", :role "Airport location", :contact nil, :evidence "working at YYJ"}], :financials [{:item "Training Expenses", :amount_or_terms "At Contractor's expense", :evidence "Such training will be provided at the Contractor's expense"} {:item "Collected Monies", :amount_or_terms "Exclusive property of the VAA; held in trust by Contractor", :evidence "All Monies collected will be the exclusive property of the VAA and will be held in trust by the Contractor for the VAA."}], :summary_points ["The Contractor is responsible for comprehensive personnel training, including customer service, technical equipment operation, and 12 hours of on-the-job training." "Mandatory Sensitivity Training and compliance with Personnel Training Regulations for the Assistance of Persons with Disabilities are required within 60 days of duty commencement." "All Contractor employees must be trained by VAA to possess and carry a Landside ID (LID) while working at the airport." "All parking revenue collected by the Contractor is the legal property of the Victoria Airport Authority and must be held in trust."]}} {:page-number 89, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 89\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 20 of 67 \n \n3.1.2 All Monies accumulated from the operation of the Parking Facilities will be collected, counted in a secure \nlocation and deposited not less than once each week to the Contractor's bank account. All Monies and Sales \nTaxes collected will be forwarded to VAA no later than the 5th business day of the following month, along \nwith the operator’s required monthly accounting to VAA.  VAA will be responsible for remitting any required \nSales Taxes to the taxing authority. \n \n3.1.3 The Contractor will be responsible for producing the following financial reports, in addition to monthly and \nannual reports as described elsewhere in this Contract, and providing the same by email to the VAA at \naccountsreceivable@victoriaairport.com:  \ni. All Revenue and Sales Taxes collected directly by the successful Proponent,  \nii. All credit card processing fees incurred by the successful proponent,     \niii. All Revenue and Sales Taxes deposited directly into VAA’s bank account, and \niv. All credit card processing fees incurred by VAA for revenues deposited directly into the VAA’s \nbank account. \n \n3.1.4 The Contractor will also be responsible for providing to the Authority the following financial reports, and \nproviding the same by email to the VAA at accountsreceivable@victoriaairport.com: \ni. Weekly Statement of Revenue providing details of all Revenues earned related to the parking \nfacilities by Revenue type and lot,  \nii. Employee Shift Schedules and Hours of Work (upon request),  \niii. List of current employees (monthly),  \niv. Additional revenue or expense reports as specified by VAA, and \nv. Details of any collection or invoicing challenges encountered related to the invoicing for Employee \nParking or Monthly Parking passes in Lot 1 or Lot 2.  \nvi. And any other reports that the VAA may require from time to time.  \n \n3.2 FINANCIAL CONTROLS & INTERNAL AUDIT PROCEDURES \n \n3.2.1 The Contractor will, throughout the Term of this Contract, develop and maintain accounting, cash control \nsystems and internal audit procedures, acceptable to and as may be required by the VAA from time to time, \nand which will include but not be limited to the following: \n \na) Segregation of duties such that cash collection, deposit and reconciliation will each be performed by \ndifferent personnel; \n \nb) Conducting monthly internal audits, including covert audits and notifying the VAA of all internal audit \nresults, including whether or not any infraction is found; \n \nc) Auditing the cash of each lot attendant, on a random basis and without notice, at least once per \nmonth and reporting to the VAA the results of these audits; and \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Weekly Deposit Deadline", :date nil, :time nil, :evidence "deposited not less than once each week to the Contractor's bank account"} {:name "Monthly Remittance Deadline", :date nil, :time nil, :evidence "no later than the 5th business day of the following month"} {:name "Internal Audit Frequency", :date nil, :time nil, :evidence "Conducting monthly internal audits"} {:name "Lot Attendant Cash Audit Frequency", :date nil, :time nil, :evidence "at least once per month"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority (VAA)", :contact "accountsreceivable@victoriaairport.com", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS... accountsreceivable@victoriaairport.com"} {:name "The Contractor", :role "Successful Proponent/Operator", :contact nil, :evidence "All Monies accumulated from the operation of the Parking Facilities will be collected... by the Contractor."} {:name "Taxing authority", :role "Recipient of Sales Taxes", :contact nil, :evidence "VAA will be responsible for remitting any required Sales Taxes to the taxing authority."}], :financials [{:item "Monies and Sales Taxes Remittance", :amount_or_terms "Forwarded to VAA no later than the 5th business day of the following month", :evidence "All Monies and Sales Taxes collected will be forwarded to VAA no later than the 5th business day of the following month"} {:item "Credit card processing fees", :amount_or_terms "Reporting required for fees incurred by proponent and VAA", :evidence "All credit card processing fees incurred by the successful proponent... All credit card processing fees incurred by VAA"} {:item "Cash Deposits", :amount_or_terms "Not less than once each week", :evidence "deposited not less than once each week to the Contractor's bank account"} {:item "Sales Tax Remittance", :amount_or_terms "VAA responsible for remitting to taxing authority", :evidence "VAA will be responsible for remitting any required Sales Taxes to the taxing authority."}], :summary_points ["The Contractor must deposit parking revenues at least weekly and remit all collected funds and taxes to the VAA by the 5th business day of the following month." "Comprehensive financial reporting is required, including weekly revenue statements, credit card fee tracking, and monthly employee lists." "The Contractor is mandated to implement strict financial controls, including segregation of duties and monthly internal/covert audits." "VAA maintains oversight through random monthly audits of lot attendants and the right to request additional revenue or expense reports."]}} {:page-number 90, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 90\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 21 of 67 \n \n \nd) Auditing, on a random basis, a minimum of ten percent (10%) of all transactions from the selected \nday. As a minimum, such audits will include a count of tickets and reconciliation of tickets to \ntransactions on the transaction ledger in terms of transaction numbers and values to ensure all \ntickets are accounted for and values are appropriate. \n \n3.2.2 The Contractor will adhere to and perform the general financial controls, including all operational controls \nand audit procedures detailed in its Proposal dated __________, 2025, and which Proposal is attached to \nand forms an integral part of this Contract at Schedule ‘B’, Appendix ‘C’ - CONTRACTOR’S PROPOSAL, or as \notherwise agreed to between the parties, from time to time.  The Contractor further agrees to comply with \nall reasonable directives from the VAA regarding acceptable accounting, cash control systems and internal \naudit procedures. \n \n3.2.3 The Contractor further agrees and covenants that any failure to comply with this Clause 3.2 will constitute \na breach of the conditions of this Contract and the Contract may be subject to the termination pursuant to \nClause GC 4.2 of Schedule 'E' - TERMINATION FOR CAUSE. \n \n3.3 FINANCIAL LOSS \n \n3.3.1 The Contractor will be responsible for the loss of all Monies and the Contractor assumes the entire \nresponsibility and liability for and will indemnify and save harmless the VAA from and against any and all \nloss, damage or expense which is not otherwise indemnified under the Contractor's insurance as set out in \nClause 2.1 of Schedule 'D' of this Contract – INSURANCE, arising out of or alleged to have arisen out of or \nconnected directly or indirectly with any act or omission of the Contractor, whether accidental, negligent, \nor deliberate; and such loss, damage or expense to include full solicitor and client fees and disbursements \nincurred by the VAA to enforce this indemnity. Neither this indemnity, nor any action taken by the VAA to \nenforce its rights under this indemnity will restrict in any way the right of the VAA to terminate this Contract \npursuant to Clause GC 4.2 of Schedule 'E' - TERMINATION FOR CAUSE, or to exercise its rights under GC \n7.1.4 of Schedule 'E' - INDEMNIFICATION. \n \n3.4 INSPECTION AND AUDIT \n \n3.4.1 The Contractor will keep, or cause to be kept in good order at its principal office in British Columbia, full, \ntrue and accurate records, entries and accounts of all Gross Revenue collected from the Parking Facilities, \nand all expenses incurred/paid by the Contractor with respect to the Work performed under this Contract \nfor each Contract Year or part thereof. Such records, entries and accounts will be maintained in accordance \nwith good business practices and principles and generally accepted Canadian accounting principles and the \nContractor will maintain such records, entries and accounts for at least one (1) year after the expiration or \ntermination of this Contract. \n \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Proposal Date Year", :date "2025", :evidence "Proposal dated __________, 2025"} {:name "Record Retention Deadline", :evidence "maintain such records, entries and accounts for at least one (1) year after the expiration or termination of this Contract."}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / VAA", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY"} {:name "VAA", :role "Authority", :evidence "The Contractor further agrees to comply with all reasonable directives from the VAA"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "The Contractor will adhere to and perform the general financial controls"}], :financials [{:item "Random Audit Requirement", :amount_or_terms "minimum of ten percent (10%) of all transactions from the selected day", :evidence "Auditing, on a random basis, a minimum of ten percent (10%) of all transactions from the selected day."} {:item "Indemnification for Financial Loss", :amount_or_terms "Contractor assumes entire responsibility and liability for loss of all Monies; includes solicitor/client fees and disbursements", :evidence "The Contractor will be responsible for the loss of all Monies and the Contractor assumes the entire responsibility and liability for and will indemnify and save harmless the VAA from and against any and all loss, damage or expense... such loss, damage or expense to include full solicitor and client fees and disbursements"} {:item "General Financial Controls", :amount_or_terms "Adherence to procedures in Proposal, Schedule ‘B’, Appendix ‘C’", :evidence "The Contractor will adhere to and perform the general financial controls, including all operational controls and audit procedures detailed in its Proposal... at Schedule ‘B’, Appendix ‘C’"} {:item "Gross Revenue and Expense Records", :amount_or_terms "Records for each Contract Year maintained in accordance with GAAP", :evidence "accurate records, entries and accounts of all Gross Revenue collected... and all expenses incurred/paid by the Contractor... in accordance with good business practices and principles and generally accepted Canadian accounting principles"}], :summary_points ["The Contractor is required to perform random audits on at least 10% of daily transactions, reconciling tickets against the transaction ledger." "Financial loss, regardless of whether it is accidental, negligent, or deliberate, is the sole responsibility of the Contractor, who must indemnify the VAA." "Failure to comply with financial and audit controls constitutes a breach of contract and may lead to termination for cause under Clause GC 4.2." "The Contractor must maintain accurate financial records in British Columbia for at least one year following the contract's expiration or termination."]}} {:page-number 91, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 91\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 22 of 67 \n \n3.4.2 The VAA will be entitled during the Term of this Contract, and for a period of twelve (12) months after \nexpiration or termination of this Contract, at its own expense, at all such times as it in its sole discretion \nconsiders necessary and appropriate to inspect, audit and make copies of any and all information in the \nContractor's records relating to the Work under this Contract, including all performance requirements and \nlevel of customer service provided, and the Contractor will cooperate with all such inspections and audits. \n \n3.4.3 Notwithstanding Clause 3.4.2 above, the VAA also reserves the right at any time during the Term of this \nContract, and for a period of twelve (12) months after expiration or termination of this Contract, at its own \nexpense, to hire an independent consultant knowledgeable of auditing airport parking operations to \nconduct an  audit of the records, entries, and accounts of the Contractor relating to the Work performed \nhereunder. The report resulting from such independent audit will be final and binding upon both the VAA \nand the Contractor, and forthwith after receipt thereof by the VAA, the VAA will repay to the Contractor \nany overpayment which may have been made by the Contractor, and the Contractor will on demand pay \nto the VAA any deficiency, as the case may be. \n \n3.4.4 If as a result of an inspection or audit, as provided for in Clause 3.4.2 or Clause 3.4.3 hereof, the VAA \ndetermines in its sole discretion acting reasonably that the Contractor has Understated Gross Revenue \nunder this Contract, the Understated Gross Revenue will be immediately due and payable by the Contractor \nto the VAA, together with Interest thereon, from the date of the inspection or audit as the case may be. In \naddition, if the Understated Gross Revenue is found to be understated by one per cent (1%) or more, the \nentire expense of the inspection or audit incurred by the VAA will be immediately due and payable by the \nContractor to the VAA together with Interest thereon, from the date of the inspection or audit as the case \nmay be. The Contractor acknowledges that the terms and provisions of this Clause 3.4.4 will have \napplication on each occurrence of Understated Gross Revenue. Notwithstanding the foregoing, in the event \nof Understated Gross Revenue as aforesaid, the VAA will be entitled to terminate this Contract pursuant to \nClause GC 4.2 of Schedule 'E' - TERMINATION FOR CAUSE and/or seek any and all other remedies it may \nhave against the Contractor pursuant to this Contract or at law. \n \n \nPART 4 PARKING BUILDINGS, EQUIPMENT & FACILITIES \n \n4.1 BUILDINGS \n \n4.1.1 The VAA will be solely responsible for providing such booths or buildings within the Parking Facilities as in \nthe VAA's reasonable opinion are necessary for the performance of the Work by the Contractor under this \nContract. \n \n4.1.2 The VAA will be solely responsible for providing electrical energy, space heat, air conditioning and \nventilation to such booths or buildings within the Parking Facilities and subject always to the provisions of \nClause GC 6.2 of Schedule 'E' - LIABILITY FOR INJURY AND/OR DAMAGE, for all structural, mechanical, and \n", :page-facts {:dates [{:name "Audit Rights Period After Expiration", :date nil, :time nil, :evidence "for a period of twelve (12) months after expiration or termination of this Contract"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority (VAA)", :contact nil, :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider / Auditee", :contact nil, :evidence "the Contractor will cooperate with all such inspections and audits."} {:name "Independent Consultant", :role "Auditor", :contact nil, :evidence "hire an independent consultant knowledgeable of auditing airport parking operations to conduct an audit"}], :financials [{:item "Understated Gross Revenue", :amount_or_terms "Immediately due and payable plus Interest", :evidence "the Understated Gross Revenue will be immediately due and payable by the Contractor to the VAA, together with Interest thereon"} {:item "Audit Expense Penalty", :amount_or_terms "Entire expense of audit due if revenue is understated by 1% or more", :evidence "if the Understated Gross Revenue is found to be understated by one per cent (1%) or more, the entire expense of the inspection or audit incurred by the VAA will be immediately due and payable"} {:item "Audit Overpayment", :amount_or_terms "VAA will repay any overpayment made by the Contractor", :evidence "the VAA will repay to the Contractor any overpayment which may have been made by the Contractor"} {:item "Utility Costs (Booths/Buildings)", :amount_or_terms "VAA responsible for electrical energy, space heat, air conditioning and ventilation", :evidence "The VAA will be solely responsible for providing electrical energy, space heat, air conditioning and ventilation to such booths or buildings"}], :summary_points ["The VAA maintains the right to audit the Contractor's records during the contract term and for 12 months following its conclusion." "Financial discrepancies found during audits require immediate settlement; understating revenue by 1% or more triggers a penalty where the Contractor must pay for the audit costs." "The VAA is responsible for providing necessary buildings/booths and the associated utility costs (power, HVAC) for the parking operations." "Reports from independent auditors hired by the VAA are considered final and binding on both parties."]}} {:page-number 92, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 92\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 23 of 67 \n \nelectrical repairs to such booths or buildings. \n \n4.1.3 The Contractor will be solely responsible for keeping such booths or buildings in a neat and tidy condition, \nincluding without limitation cleaning the booths or buildings and the interior and exterior surfaces of all \nwindows, collecting and placing all debris, refuse and recyclable materials in containers designated by the \nVAA. \n \n4.1.4. The Contractor will use the buildings, booths and Parking Equipment provided by the VAA for the operation \nof the Parking Facilities and related services and for no other purpose unless prior written approval is \nobtained from the VAA. \n \n4.2 PARKING EQUIPMENT \n \n4.2.1 The list of Parking Equipment provided by the VAA is attached to the RFP as Appendix D – PARKING \nEQUIPMENT LIST, and the Parking Equipment described therein is the absolute property of the VAA. \n \n4.2.2 The Contractor will be responsible for monitoring and reporting issues and for doing maintenance of \nequipment inside the booth, excluding SKIDATA-related Parking Equipment.  Preventative maintenance of \nthe Parking Equipment will be performed by others, but the Contractor may be asked to assist while \ntroubleshooting issues. \n \n4.2.3 The Contractor will carry out daily visual inspections of the Parking Equipment to ensure proper operation \nand will immediately notify the VAA if there are problems with Parking Equipment for which the VAA is \nresponsible. \n \n4.2.4 The Contractor will not reset the counters on any Parking Equipment, so equipped, at any time unless \nrequested to do so by the VAA. \n \n4.2.5 The Contractor will monitor for Parking Equipment breakdown and will report issues to maintenance \ncontractor for resolution. \n \n4.3 PARKING FACILITIES  \n \n4.3.1 The Parking Facilities consist of the following facilities, all as more particularly shown on the drawing \nreferred to as, “Internal Version”, attached to the RFP as Appendix A – YYJ PARKING FACILITIES: \n \n[SEE TABLE ON NEXT PAGE] \n  \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / Owner (VAA)", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Authority / Owner", :evidence "containers designated by the VAA."} {:name "SKIDATA", :role "Parking Equipment Provider/Manufacturer", :evidence "excluding SKIDATA-related Parking Equipment."}], :financials [], :summary_points ["The Contractor is responsible for the cleanliness and basic maintenance of parking booths and buildings, including window cleaning and waste management." "Parking structures and equipment provided by the VAA must be used exclusively for parking operations unless otherwise approved in writing." "The Contractor is tasked with monitoring equipment, performing daily visual inspections, and reporting breakdowns to the designated maintenance contractor." "Preventative maintenance of parking equipment is performed by third parties, though the Contractor may be required to assist in troubleshooting."]}} {:page-number 93, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 93\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 24 of 67 \n \n \nFacility # of spaces (approximate) \nShort Term Lot  166 \nLong Term Lot 1  1,405 \nLong Term Lot 2 comprised of the following:  \nOrange Lot 509 \nPurple Lot 195 \nRed Lot 274 \nBrown Lot 303 \nEmployee Lot 391 \nTotal Spaces 3,243 \n \n4.3.2 Subject always to the provisions of Clause GC 6.2 of Schedule 'E' - LIABILITY FOR INJURY AND/OR DAMAGE, \nthe responsibilities of the Contractor and the VAA for maintenance and repair of the Parking Facilities will \nbe in accordance with Schedule ‘B’, Appendix 'A' – PARKING FACILITIES – MAINTENANC & REPAIR \nRESPONSIBILITIES, attached hereto. \n \n4.3.3 Subject always to the provisions of Clause GC 6.2 of Schedule 'E' - LIABILITY FOR INJURY AND/OR DAMAGE, \nthe VAA will be responsible, at its sole expense, for providing, maintaining and repairing, all utilities to, at, \nupon and within the Parking Facilities, including without limitation internet connection, drainage, electrical, \nsewer, structural and water. \n \n4.3.4 The design, production, and installation of any signs, promotional items, brochures, and way-finding related \nto the Parking Facilities will be the responsibility of the VAA, and at the VAA’s sole discretion and expense. \n \n4.3.5 The VAA will provide and repair the baggage carts and corrals in the Parking Facilities. \n \n4.3.6 The VAA will be responsible at its sole cost and expense for providing all directional signage, Parking Fee \nsigns, and all operational instructions related to payment of the Parking Fees. \n \n4.3.7 The Contractor will not install signs of any nature, including advertising signs, in the Parking Facilities, \nwithout the prior written approval of the VAA. \n \n  \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Authority / Owner (VAA)", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Authority / Owner", :evidence "the responsibilities of the Contractor and the VAA"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "the responsibilities of the Contractor and the VAA for maintenance and repair"}], :financials [{:item "Utilities maintenance and repair", :amount_or_terms "VAA's sole expense", :evidence "the VAA will be responsible, at its sole expense, for providing, maintaining and repairing, all utilities"} {:item "Signage, promotional items, and way-finding", :amount_or_terms "VAA's sole expense", :evidence "design, production, and installation of any signs... will be the responsibility of the VAA, and at the VAA’s sole discretion and expense."} {:item "Directional and Parking Fee signs", :amount_or_terms "VAA's sole cost and expense", :evidence "The VAA will be responsible at its sole cost and expense for providing all directional signage, Parking Fee signs"}], :summary_points ["The parking facilities consist of approximately 3,243 total spaces distributed across Short Term, Long Term, and Employee lots." "Maintenance and repair responsibilities are divided between the Contractor and VAA as detailed in Clause GC 6.2 and Schedule ‘B’, Appendix 'A'." "VAA is solely responsible for the cost and provision of all utilities, baggage carts, and signage (including promotional and fee-related) within the facilities." "The Contractor is prohibited from installing any signs or advertising without the VAA's prior written approval."]}} {:page-number 94, :page-text "SOURCE PAGE 94\n VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS \n 2025 Parking Management Services \n \n   \n \n Page 25 of 67 \n \n \nAPPENDIX 'A' \nPARKING FACILITIES \nMAINTENANCE & REPAIR RESPONSIBILITIES \n \nPursuant to Clause 4.3.2 of this Schedule ‘B’ - PARKING FACILITIES, the responsibilities of the \nContractor and the VAA are as follows: \n \nItem Responsibility  \nContractor    VAA  \nBaggage Carts, Corrals & Canopies    \nIce Control (refer to the map)     \nLandscaping    \nLighting    \nParking Equipment and Computer Equipment     \nOil Stain Removal & Oil Spill Cleanup     \nPaved Surfaces, including crack filling    \nPavement Markings     \nSidewalks & Curbs (including snow removal and ice control)    \nSignage     \nSnow Removal (refer to map) see Note     \nSurface Drains, Catch Basins, Oil Separators     \nVegetation & Weed Control (pavement surfaces only)   \n \nNOTES: \nNote   Off-site location for snow dump site to be identified by VAA upon requirement. \n \n \n  \n", :page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY", :role "Authority / VAA", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Contractor", :role "Service Provider", :evidence "responsibilities of the Contractor and the VAA are as follows"}], :financials [], :summary_points ["The table defines specific maintenance and repair responsibilities allocated between the Contractor and the Victoria Airport Authority 