ment company to provide services for Victoria International Airport (YYJ)." "The airport parking infrastructure consists of 3,243 total spaces, divided into public daily (2,686), short-term (166), and employee (391) lots." "YYJ is primarily an Origin and Destination airport and was the third busiest in British Columbia in 2018 with 2 million passengers." "VAA acknowledges its operations are on the traditional territories of the W̱SÁNEĆ people and is committed to partnering with local First Nations."]} {:dates [], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Issuing Authority", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "VAA", :role "Issuing Authority", :evidence "VAA encourages innovation"} {:name "Victoria International Airport", :role "Site Location", :evidence "manage the Parking Facilities at Victoria International Airport"}], :financials [], :summary_points ["The procurement seeks a parking management company to manage four primary lots totaling over 3,200 spaces plus seasonal overflow and curbside activities." "Proponents are expected to have expertise in airport parking operations, curb management, and current technological trends." "The scope includes developing and implementing a Curbside Management Program for terminal frontage and commercial lanes." "A forthcoming terminal expansion project is noted as a factor that will likely impact future parking configurations and operations."]} {:dates [{:name "Contract Commencement Date", :date "2025-06-01", :evidence "commencing June 1st, 2025"} {:name "Contract End Date", :date "2030-05-31", :evidence "ending on May 31st, 2030"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / Issuer of RFP", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Victoria International Airport", :role "Location of Services", :evidence "Parking Facilities the successful Proponent will be responsible for at the Victoria International Airport"}], :financials [