ies for Indigenous business engagement, skills training and employment"}], :financials [{:item "Employee Wages", :amount_or_terms "Greater than the BC provincial minimum wage, plus benefits", :evidence "Pay employees greater that the BC provincial minimum wage, plus benefits."}], :summary_points ["The successful Proponent is responsible for all aspects of employment, including recruitment, training, and performance management for the 2025 Parking Management Services." "Operational requirements include a local office presence, 20-hour daily staffing for Lot 1 booths, and 15.5-hour daily curb management coverage." "Proponents are encouraged to include opportunities for Indigenous business engagement and skills training in their proposals." "All staff must be legally able to work in Canada, be fluent in English, and be paid above the B.C. provincial minimum wage."]}}, :duration-ms 4090, :usage {:prompt-tokens 1238, :completion-tokens 720, :total-tokens 1958}, :inputs #:ai.obney.orc.orc-service.core.todo-processors{:map-each-index 6, :map-each-parent #uuid "621004b8-f33b-41f9-a358-7262f91a88d9"}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "c46d393b-eb8a-4120-accf-5eca706684c4", :sheet-id #uuid "120307da-6e8f-4362-aaa2-56bae5f6aa7f", :timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-21T16:23:04.359716-05:00"} {:tick-id #uuid "ad74ce10-75ff-4da7-9deb-78e649764531", :writes {:page-facts {:dates [], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Authority / Issuing Body", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Canadian Transportation Agency (CTA)", :role "Auditor", :evidence "periodic audits conducted by the Canadian Transportation Agency (CTA)"} {:name "VAA", :role "Authority", :evidence "Additional VAA-required and administered training includes"} {:name "Victoria International Airport", :role "Airport Location", :evidence "promote inclusivity at Victoria International Airport"}], :financials [{:item "Training Expenses", :amount_or_terms "At the su