ation will be conducted by an evaluation committee made up of Authority employees and its agents."}], :financials [{:item "Operational Establishment Costs", :amount_or_terms "Sole responsibility of the successful Proponent; must not be passed on to the Authority", :evidence "Any costs associated with establishing operations in the Parking Facilities will be the sole responsibility of the successful Proponent and must not be passed on to the Authority."} {:item "Financial Evaluation Criteria", :amount_or_terms "Includes capital investment potential, profit sharing, and financial stability", :evidence "The Proponent’s financial plan including capital investment potential and profit sharing... The Proponent’s financial stability."}], :summary_points ["The successful Proponent is responsible for all transition and operational establishment costs, which cannot be billed to the Victoria Airport Authority." "Proposals will be evaluated by a committee based on service quality, relevant experience, local market presence, and financial stability." "Staffing evaluation emphasizes recruitment, retention, compensation programs, and training, including opportunities for Indigenous business engagement and skills training." "Proponents must demonstrate knowledge of safety standards as defined by the Canadian Centre for Occupational Health and Safety (CCOHS)."]} {:dates [{:name "Minimum business experience deadline", :date "2025-06-01", :evidence "parking management business for a minimum of five (5) years immediately prior to June 1st, 2025"} {:name "Debriefing request deadline", :evidence "request a debriefing meeting within thirty (30) days of receiving notification"}], :entities [{:name "Victoria Airport Authority", :role "Issuing Authority", :evidence "VICTORIA AIRPORT AUTHORITY - REQUEST FOR PROPOSALS"} {:name "Victoria International Airport", :role "Presentation Location", :contact "2nd floor of the Air Terminal Building (1640 Electra Blvd)", :evidence "onsite presentation wo